  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1254 PM MDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nEast Idaho remains under the influence of trough draped over the\nPacNW today, behind surface frontal boundary that moved through\novernight. Winds remain breezy today in post frontal atmosphere,\nand temperatures remain significantly cooler than yesterday.\nHigh-res models indicating potential for a sprinkle this\nafternoon as the trough approaches, with a better signal for a\nbrief light shower this evening and overnight in portions of the\neastern highlands. Have nudged QPF and PoP up slightly from NBM\nconsensus forecast overnight. Temps do warm up slightly for\nSunday, but precipitation forecast has shifted slightly to have\nbetter confidence during the overnight Sunday night and into\nMonday. From there, ensembles still favor rebuilding a shallow\nridge over Idaho into the end of the week. Temperatures remain\nnear normal for most of the week, but warm up late in the weak\nahead of potential trough arriving over the weekend. There are\ncluster differences in timing and depth, so confidence remains\nlow for now on temperature and precipitation trends heading into\nnext weekend.",
